<title>FRANCE: HORSE RACING-FRENCH DERBY DAY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-FRENCH DERBY DAY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>CHANTILLY, France 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of group one</p>
<p>races on French Derby day on Sunday:</p>
<p>Prix Jean Prat (for three-year-olds), run over nine furlongs</p>
<p>(1.8 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Starborough	  (ridden by Frankie Dettori)</p>
<p> 2. Mamalik		(Richard Hills)</p>
<p> 3. Kirkwall	     (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p> 4. Visionary	    (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>Five ran.</p>
<p>Distances: A length and a half, short head, nose.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Sheikh Mohammed and trained in England by</p>
<p>David Loder.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: $75,420.</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (including a one-franc stake): Win 3.00; places</p>
<p>2.10, 3.60. Straight Forecast 14.80.</p>
<p>Prix du Jockey-Club (French Derby) (for three-year-olds),</p>
<p>run over one 12 furlongs (2.4 km):</p>
<p> 1. Peintre Celebre	(Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p> 2. Oscar		    (Sylvain Guillot)</p>
<p> 3. Astrabad		 (Gerald Mosse)</p>
<p> 4. Fragrant Mix	   (Thierry Jarnet)</p>
<p>14 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Two lengths, half a length, four lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Daniel Wildenstein and trained in France by</p>
<p>Andre Fabre.</p>
<p>Value to the winner: $471,321</p>
<p>Pari-Mutuel (includes a one-franc stake): Win 4.10; places</p>
<p>2.10, 3.10, 4.20. Dual Forecast 25.70.</p>
</text>
